      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2a4df969e04460cfc5e29d|full_name} From what I understand this canny was marked complete. But _not_ because the crash in that example world was fixed. Crashing in that world is still possible until the world is updated.\nThe menu does not cause the crash. Like you said, the menu close does not always cause it to happen. But also, it’s not the only way to cause it to happen. So this canny was kept marked as complete. More detail in the screenshot. (I think your canny was turned into a menu hitch canny and not a crash canny? Maybe? Or at the very least it should just be closed, I guess. Again, more detail in the screenshot.)\nThe crash issue is still being worked on, and may not make it into this release. Stop using resync, even though the SDK warns you if you don’t use it. And tell the world authors of worlds you are in to stop using it too. Because that’s the only way this information is communicated. And, developers and others have indicated to me it was common knowledge it frequently crashed. This knowledge is not in the docs and the SDK offers misleading encouragement. We need more people sharing these sorts of facts about the SDK. Because I didn’t even know. And I use the feature weekly. I have for months. That history of use along with the SDK message (and wanting synchronized audio at a party for the first time in 4 years) is why I felt safe using it at my party.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
